    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.25) and **Bryson Stott** (72.63) anchor our lineup as the only two hitters exceeding the 70-point threshold. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an elite start despite facing a left-handed arm in Rod\u00f3n, as his dynamic platoon profile and prime spot in the two-hole insulate his floor. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** draws the most favorable matchup of the day against Scherzer (5.32 xERA); his 19% SP skill boost and positive platoon splits make him a primary engine for our category accumulation. **Lawrence Butler** also warrants attention with a strong 67.98 score, benefiting significantly from a neutral-to-favorable matchup against Sproat where his right-handed power profile is expected to play up.\n\nConversely, we are fading the bottom of our starting corps as we navigate the \"marginal\" territory of our roster. **Jonathan Aranda**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** are all fighting through negative platoon splits against Griffin, leaving them in the 42\u201349 point range\u2014starts strictly by necessity due to our daily game cap management. **Gavin Sheets** sits on the edge of \"Strong\" at 57.03; while he benefits from hitting cleanup, his negative BvP history against Singer prevents a higher projection. The most difficult bench decision involved **Masyn Winn** (45.59). While **Masyn Winn** provides the speed we covet to address our scarcity in SB, he narrowly missed the cut because the projected run-scoring environment for the rest of the utility-capable hitters outperformed his specific matchup against Warren.\n\nRegarding risk management, we remain cautious of the volatility inherent in our current OF structure, particularly as we await the return of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** from the IL, both of whom remain sidelined. Our depth pieces\u2014including **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014are currently being held in reserve to ensure we do not hit our total game caps before more favorable matchups arise. No significant weather-related warnings are impacting the slate, but we are monitoring the lineup for **Jonathan Aranda** and others closely, as any drop in the batting order would likely force an immediate re-evaluation of their sub-50 efficiency scores.",
